 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The damsel of the Isaurian nation\nMade her young husband's love immortalize thee,\nTo me it is but a laughing one.\nYea, I have seen my lady; many,\nIn truth all in vain, shall try away\nMy wilful love and this long expectation\nOf any real union - she remains,\nThough used to face death alone. Away!\nOh, well may those fair faces decay,\nAnd greyish hair grow with milder decay!\nEvil luck and misfortune make delay\nFor sweet come-upon. The world away,",
